KG42.register("clusters-ecde018854d949b9483e7790",{"id":"08-real_time_prices::v142-d-CL001","paper":"08-real_time_prices","label":"Bid-free price-responsive participation by small consumers and DER","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL001","label":"Bid-free price-responsive participation by small consumers and DER","market_meaning":"Small consumers and small DER participate in EcoGrid by receiving TSO real-time prices and autonomously adjusting electricity consumption or generation, without submitting market bids or schedules. The metering conditions of the specified implementation are linked to the price interval; participants have no performance obligation to deliver the balancing response expected by the TSO, and the proposed restriction to small entities applies only if adopted.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","participation","coordination"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The five-minute condition belongs to the specified implementation, while adaptations for longer metering intervals remain retained. The anti-arbitrage participation restriction is conditional on adoption by the TSO. In the original text, prosumers encompasses consumers and producers, whereas the frozen participation.prosumer focuses on entities capable of supply; the two types of participation nodes are therefore retained separately. The absence of a performance obligation applies only to the expected response in Eq. (2) and does not extend to exemption from electricity-volume settlement.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"Exemption from submitting bids or schedules and response to received prices jointly constitute a participation rule with independent significance; metering and signal delivery provide implementation interfaces. Consumers and supply-capable entities constitute complementary scopes of participation. The completeness of the pricing algorithm is disclosed separately by v142-d-CL002; this cluster assembles only procedural participation conditions.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"The exemption from submitting demand bids and consumption schedules constitutes an institutional condition for consumer participation."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"The exemption from submitting supply bids complements the mode of supply-side participation and is limited to the EcoGrid real-time market."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides consumers' mode of response to received prices, metering admission requirements, and conditional participation boundaries."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the corresponding procedural conditions for small DER and supply-capable participants; retains the current C.1 content and incomplete C.2 bindings."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Shares price delivery, intervals, metering alignment, and participation boundaries; optimization-based pricing and forecasting remain primarily assigned to v142-d-CL002."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev18"],"rationale":"The same bid-free design covers demand-side and supply-side submission behavior separately, and the two are complementary; constraints on different sides are not classified as duplicate objects merely because they share a source."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev18","v141-b-g03-e07"],"rationale":"The market-level exclusion of demand submissions and consumer participation through response to received prices complement each other, forming a mode of participation that requires no bid submission, rather than adding a new admission dependency edge."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev09","v141-b-g01-ev18","v141-b-g03-e07"],"rationale":"The exclusion of supply submissions and the mode of participation in which small DER adjust production after receiving prices belong to the same EcoGrid design; this exclusion is not extended to the external RP market."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev01","v141-b-g01-ev09","v141-b-g01-ev12"],"rationale":"The source lists small end consumers and small DER together as price-responsive participants; the two chains cover entities with different demand and supply capabilities, retaining their respective nodes and constraints."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C006","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C007","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C008","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C011"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev01","v141-b-g01-ev12","v141-b-g01-ev15","v141-b-g01-ev16","v141-b-g01-ev22","v141-b-g01-ev24"],"rationale":"The TSO publishes prices directly to participants in advance, enabling consumers to respond to them; alignment of price and metering intervals corresponds to the metering admission condition of the specified implementation. This mapping connects only existing activities and conditions."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CON006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C008","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C011","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C012"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev01","v141-b-g01-ev12","v141-b-g01-ev22","v141-b-g01-ev24"],"rationale":"The real-time prices published to participants also serve as inputs to autonomous responses by small DER; the source supports the linkage between signal delivery and participation activities but does not guarantee that the actual response reaches the quantity expected by the TSO."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R005::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R006::V::coordination.price_signal"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R004::V::coordination.price_signal","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev01","v141-b-g01-ev09","v141-b-g01-ev22"],"rationale":"The three chains refer to the same EcoGrid real-time price coordination function, with R004 selected solely as the display representative. All original references and the nodes, edges, and participation conditions for different recipients continue to be retained."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-GAP001","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B evidence used in this cluster remains unverified and is eligible only to provide experimental candidate support; assembled indicates only that the procedural scope described above can be assembled, not that the sources or scientific interpretations have undergone independent review.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev01","v141-b-g01-ev09","v141-b-g01-ev15","v141-b-g01-ev16","v141-b-g01-ev18","v141-b-g01-ev22","v141-b-g01-ev24","v141-b-g01-ev30","v141-b-g02-ev-16","v141-b-g03-e07"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check the original text, scope of entities, conditions, and citation locations item by item, and examine all inter-chain mappings; the output of this round must not be treated as the result of a B audit or an independent C.2 review."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-GAP002","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The bid-free mode of participation and metering conditions are currently attached to existing submission, participation, and coordination nodes; the related node proposals remain unapproved. This limitation does not prevent the procedural candidate from being formed, but it does not support merging consumer-type and supply-capable entity nodes.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R002::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C007","v141-c-R005::V::participation.consumer","v141-c-R006::V::participation.prosumer"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev09","v141-b-g01-ev15","v141-b-g01-ev16","v141-b-g01-ev18"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-prop01","v141-b-g01-prop03"],"required_work":"Manually assess whether the participation-mode and metering concepts require an ontology extension; if adopted, revise the upstream version separately, while retaining the original objects in this round."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-GAP003","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R006 has empty current_C2_bindings, and the current revision request retains the C2_nonmathematical_has_math issue. This cluster uses only its existing procedural facts and does not thereby claim that the response mathematics or C.2 bindings are complete.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C003","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C004"],"evidence_ids":[],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently, explicitly check and complete the bindings between procedural facts and frozen graph objects at the C layer; if mathematical formalization is required, propose a separate source-supported revision rather than having D infer and supply it."}]},"rule_refs":["08-real_time_prices::v141-c-R001","08-real_time_prices::v141-c-R002","08-real_time_prices::v141-c-R005","08-real_time_prices::v141-c-R006","08-real_time_prices::v141-c-R004"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-42adfdfb6dfa84b0","COMP-5662f1d03d6b9b67","COMP-5e870d267afec9a0","COMP-ab3d11c48c98c7be","COMP-f66e9ec7493cbb66","KG31-c53b1d455f59fded"]});
